# Mockito's default (inline) mock maker installs a Byte Buddy agent by
# self-attaching to the running JVM. That attach is blocked on this machine —
# every Mockito test failed with "Could not self-attach to current VM using
# external process" before this file existed, including the ones that predate it.
#
# The subclass mock maker needs no agent. The cost is that it cannot mock final
# classes, final methods or statics; nothing in this suite does, and if that
# changes the alternative is -Djdk.attach.allowAttachSelf=true on the surefire
# argLine rather than reverting this.
mock-maker-subclass
